Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] media: simaai-v4l2-video: validate a channel's link on its own stream

The DMA bridge routes channel N from its sink pad N, stream N, to its source
pad VDMA_CHANNELS + N, stream N. v4l2vid_link_validate() asks the source pad
for the format of stream 0, so only channel 0 validates. A capture node of
channel 1 to 3 fails STREAMON with -EPIPE although its format matches, and a
CSI port carries one virtual channel. Ask for the format of the channel's own
stream.

---
 drivers/media/platform/simaai/simaai-v4l2-video.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/simaai/simaai-v4l2-video.c b/drivers/media/platform/simaai/simaai-v4l2-video.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/simaai/simaai-v4l2-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/simaai/simaai-v4l2-video.c
@@ -756,6 +756,13 @@
 
 	source_fmt.which = V4L2_SUBDEV_FORMAT_ACTIVE;
 	source_fmt.pad = link->source->index;
+	/*
+	 * The bridge routes channel N from its sink pad N, stream N, to its
+	 * source pad VDMA_CHANNELS + N, stream N. A channel past the first
+	 * carries its format on its own stream, never on stream 0.
+	 */
+	if (link->source->index >= VDMA_CHANNELS)
+		source_fmt.stream = link->source->index - VDMA_CHANNELS;
 
 	ret = v4l2_subdev_call(source_sd, pad, get_fmt, NULL, &source_fmt);
 	if (ret < 0) {
